From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Guard the optional context copy in server_select()

GCC 14 with -O3 cannot prove that context is non-null whenever the server
returns context data, and turns the memcpy() into a -Werror=nonnull failure.
The extra check is also correct for callers that pass no context.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index 18b4c2e1122..71130497b62 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -790,7 +790,7 @@ unsigned int server_select( const union select_op *select_op, data_size_t size,
     while (ret == STATUS_USER_APC || ret == STATUS_KERNEL_APC);
 
     if (ret == STATUS_USER_APC) *user_apc = reply_data.call.user;
-    if (reply_size > sizeof(reply_data.call))
+    if (context && reply_size > sizeof(reply_data.call))
     {
         memcpy( context, reply_data.context, reply_size - sizeof(reply_data.call) );
         context[0].flags &= ~SERVER_CTX_EXEC_SPACE;
